# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.net29, REST=1 (with WIFID=1), MORE_JOBS="com.apple.bluetoothd com.apple.BlueTool",
# NILINJECT=Preferences CIINJECT=Preferences, connsys_step=17, XNU_SECS=155,
# applog=1 applog_name=Preferences.
#
# Run 97 (logs/lancelot-connsys49.log) is the first picture of Settings that is not a corpse: the root
# list with the Wi-Fi row showing the joined network (Cudy_OpenWrt_2.4Ghz), and the process alive 8 s
# after the tap (it used to die at 0.57 s). The rows carry no icons there -- the nil iconImage pair is
# left out by libredwood-nil -- and so CoreImage was not asked for a context yet.
#
# This run taps the Wi-Fi row ("Wi-Fi  Cudy_OpenWrt_2.4Ghz  >" at y = 240 of 650 in that picture,
# x = 0.5) and waits for the pane: the pane's cells are where MobileIcons drew through CoreImage and
# killed the program in run 96. If it lives, the picture shows the switch and the network, and the next
# run can turn Wi-Fi off and on; if it does not, the console tail has the "!ci:" lines and the frames.
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 22
/redwood/bin/net_test dhcp en0 waitaddr en0 10
/redwood/bin/net_test fbwait 60
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 16
/redwood/bin/rwtouch swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 200
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 3
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.543 0.712
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 6
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.368
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 8
/redwood/bin/net_test procs Preferences
/redwood/bin/fbgrab -log wifi 300 0.5
/redwood/bin/net_test end